{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"section-edge-intelligence","type":"group","x":-900,"y":-600,"width":2200,"height":600,"color":"4","label":"📌 Section 1: Edge Intelligence Challenges"},
		{"id":"section-imc-challenges","type":"group","x":-900,"y":200,"width":2200,"height":600,"color":"2","label":"📌 Section 2: IMC Implementation Challenges"},
		{"id":"section-2t1c-solution","type":"group","x":-900,"y":1000,"width":2200,"height":600,"color":"6","label":"📌 Section 3: 2T1C Array Solution"},
		{"id":"main-title","type":"text","text":"# FeFET-Based Adaptive Edge Intelligence System\n\n**Visual Citation Map**","x":-500,"y":-800,"width":800,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"text-ei-continual-learning","type":"text","text":"## Continual Learning & Adaptation\n\nEI systems must continually learn new knowledge and adapt to environmental changes.\n\n**Key Challenge:** On-device adaptation when cloud unavailable.","x":-860,"y":-540,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-ei-von-neumann","type":"text","text":"## von Neumann Bottleneck\n\nTraditional hardware implementations face significant bottlenecks:\n\n• Massive data movement\n• Instruction communication\n• Majority of latency & power","x":-500,"y":-540,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-ei-imc-paradigm","type":"text","text":"## Paradigm Shift to IMC\n\nTransition toward in-memory computing architectures inspired by biological neural networks.\n\n**Key Benefit:** Eliminates data movement.","x":-140,"y":-540,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-imc-precise-weights","type":"text","text":"## Precise Weight Programming\n\n**Core Challenge:** Achieving precise weight mapping while minimizing adjustments.\n\n• Write interference constrains scalability\n• Significantly limits computational power","x":-860,"y":260,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-imc-system-overhead","type":"text","text":"## System Overhead\n\nHigh-precision weight updates require:\n\n• Additional peripheral circuits\n• Intricate control strategies\n• Increased system overhead","x":-500,"y":260,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-imc-endurance","type":"text","text":"## Device Endurance Issues\n\nFrequent program/erase cycles degrade device endurance:\n\n• Amplify non-ideal characteristics\n• Reduce overall system efficiency","x":-140,"y":260,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-imc-fefet-solution","type":"text","text":"## FeFET Solution\n\nFerroelectric transistors store information via polarization state:\n\n• Read-write separated structure\n• Hardware-software co-design\n• Bypasses cumbersome programming","x":220,"y":260,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-2t1c-isolation","type":"text","text":"## Error Isolation via Gating Transistor\n\nIncorporating a gating transistor isolates operational errors:\n\n• Avoids complex programming schemes\n• Mitigates write crosstalk","x":-860,"y":1060,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-2t1c-conductance","type":"text","text":"## Read-Write Separation\n\nLeveraging read-write separation characteristic of FeFETs:\n\n• Distinct conductance states\n• Gate modulation enables flexible weight control","x":-500,"y":1060,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-2t1c-dual-function","type":"text","text":"## Dual Functionality\n\nGating transistor serves dual purposes:\n\n1. Isolation gate during write operations\n2. Analog tuner during inference","x":-140,"y":1060,"width":320,"height":220},
		{"id":"text-2t1c-results","type":"text","text":"## Experimental Validation\n\n• 4 Kb FeFET array fabricated\n• Incremental learning on Fashion-MNIST\n• Global drift compensation with minimal overhead","x":220,"y":1060,"width":320,"height":220},
